# BAHÍA ROJA

[![make.fun · gta6-01](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![rank](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/Masriah091/bahia-roja/rank.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01/leaderboard?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![reward](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/Masriah091/bahia-roja/reward.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)

BAHÍA ROJA is an original open-world crime game built for the Make GTA 6 bounty on make.fun. You roam a sun-baked port city on foot and by car through a 15-mission campaign, outrunning a 5-star wanted system backed by a helicopter while the port dispatch calls the chase in real time. Six shop types, three save slots, a full map and pause stats round out the run.

This repository is my entry for the bounty at https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01.

## Play

Run `node serve.ts`, then open http://localhost:8080 in a desktop browser. The game lives in `game/` as plain static files — no build step, no network requests — and plays with keyboard and mouse.

## Hand-in

`node main.ts` copies `game/` and `screenshots/` into the output directory and writes `dossier.json` there via `buildDossier` from `vendor/makefun-game.ts`, then prints a one-line summary of what was handed in.

